lling the first two and dropping the rest is the defect, not partial credit: the reader cannot tell which topics are answerable by number. Never a bare number. Also use when writing any conversational reply — answering a question, reporting what was found, proposing an approach, considering asking for a decision, or asking where the work goes next. Governs length, structure, when to decide rather than ask, the decision that leads the message, the ascend/descend prompt that sends it as a message of its own, the labelled question block, and linking every issue and PR number rather than writing it bare. Loading it does not replace whatever else owns the turn: a reply reporting a handoff, an issue, a commit or a finished piece of work is still a reply, so it loads alongside that skill rather than instead of it. Does not apply to reports, issues, PRs, commits, or code comments.
